---
// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Numen Games S.L.
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
// MIS-128 — the 404 the archive owes its readers. DEUDA-404 records URL
// breakages as accepted policy ("we own it and document the 404s"); this
// page is the other half of owning it: a lost reader gets the site's own
// navigation and search instead of Cloudflare's bare error. Served by
// Workers via `not_found_handling = "404-page"` (wrangler.toml).
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="404 — Not found · Numinia"
  description="This URL answers nothing. The search and the corpus index can find what moved."
  canonicalPath="/404"
>
  <section class="pb-20 pt-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[800px] px-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[0.65rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-dim mb-4">HTTP 404</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl text-foreground mb-6">This URL answers nothing.</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4">
        The archive renames and retires documents on purpose, and some breakage
        is accepted and recorded rather than hidden — see
        <a href="/debt" class="text-accent hover:underline">the debt register</a>,
        the public register of exactly that. If a link brought you here, the
        document most likely moved.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5 mb-10 space-y-1">
        <li>Use the search in the top bar — it indexes every published page.</li>
        <li>Or start at the <a href="/" class="text-accent hover:underline">home page</a>, where the sections are listed.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-border"></span>
        <span class="font-mono text-[0.6rem] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-dim">nothing was deleted silently</span>
        <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-border"></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
